  "description": "SIJXOB crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C66 H64 Cr4 Dy4 N11 O38 1+,C6 H4 N1 O2 1-,1.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Cr3 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors; Cr4 (Cr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 2.892-4.269 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.54-157.86°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C72H71Cr4Dy4N12O41.50.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
